I park my bicycle in front of the café.
I am a little nervous.
Today is my first shift as a volunteer.
I open the door and walk directly behind the counter.
A woman with dark hair is already there.
She smiles broadly when she sees me.
"You must be Maya," she says.
"I am Elif."
"Yes, exactly," I answer.
"Nice to meet you."
Elif organizes the weekend shifts at the community café.
She points to a small room in the back.
"You can leave your jacket there," she says.
I hang up my jacket and come back.
Elif gives me a black apron.
"Welcome to the team," she says warmly.
I put the apron on.
I have never worked in a café before.
But today I am learning to make good coffee.
